.TH LIBSTRARRAY_STRARRAY_INDEX_OF_B 3 "2023-04-01" "libstrarray" "String Array Library"
.SH NAME
strarray_index_of_b \- Find the index of a string in a string array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libstrarray.h>
.B #include <lib/uint64.h>
.sp
.B int64
.B strarray_index_of_b(strarray* arr, const char* s, size_t len);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B strarray_index_of_b
function finds the index of a string in a string array. The
.B arr
argument is a pointer to a
.B strarray
structure representing the array, and the
.B s
argument is a pointer to a constant character string representing the string to search for. The
.B len
argument is a size_t representing the length of the string to search for.
The
.B strarray_index_of_b
function returns the index of the string if it is found, or -1 if it is not found.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B strarray_index_of_b
function to find the index of a string in a string array:
.nf
.B #include <libstrarray.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B #include <lib/uint64.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   strarray arr;
.B   strarray_init(&arr);
.B   strarray_append(&arr, "Hello");
.B   strarray_append(&arr, "world");
.B   int64 index = strarray_index_of_b(&arr, "world", 5);
.B   printf("Index of 'world': %ld\n", index);
.B   // Free the allocated memory
.B   strarray_done(&arr);
.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B strarray_init(3),
.B strarray_append(3),
.B strarray_done(3)